I go further into the market.
There is a spice stall there.
An elderly man is sitting in the stall.
I go near the stall.
"Kaka, hello," I say.
"Hello, madam," he says.
He shows me a small box.
"This is a special tea masala," he says.
"You smell this," he says proudly.
He gives me a pinch of masala.
I smell the masala.
The aroma is very nice.
I like it a lot.
"I want this masala," I say.
"Give me a small packet," I say.
"What is the price for this?" I ask.
"Fifty rupees," Kaka says.
I give him fifty rupees.
I put the spice packet in my cloth bag.
